entry.content:
&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Re%5C%3A+Intent+to+Ship%5C%3A+Secure+Payment+Confirmation%5C%3A+Locale+Validation%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;[blink-dev] Re: Intent to Ship: Secure Payment Confirmation: Locale Validation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Darwin+Yang%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Darwin Yang&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20261021" rel="nofollow"&gt;Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:15:48 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;That's a good point! We don't expect much use and looking at the latest UMA
data &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="http://uma/p/chrome/timeline?sid=a520566d7db7e348ab795fe27a70cdc1"&gt;http://uma/p/chrome/timeline?sid=a520566d7db7e348ab795fe27a70cdc1&lt;/a&gt;&gt;,
we see about 17 events (aggregated across 7 days) at peak. We attribute
most of this (if not all) to developers working with us on improving SPC
who are asking for this feature; therefore, the impact of this change
should be minimal.&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;


Cheers,
Darwin Yang

On Wed, Oct 21, 2026 at 11:30 AM Alex Russell &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="ff8c939698978b9386d1d1d1bf9c978d9092968a92d1908d98"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
wrote:

&gt; Thanks, Darwin.
&gt;
&gt; Vlad pointed out that this change to increase strictness implies some new
&gt; or additional breakage for sites. Do we have a sense for how often that
&gt; will trigger? Do we have any UMA data that would give us a sense for the
&gt; maximum extent of potential breakage? I.e., what's the risk?
&gt;
&gt; Best,
&gt;
&gt; Alex
&gt;
&gt; On Tuesday, October 20, 2026 at 7:35:08 AM UTC-7 Darwin Yang wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; Hi Alex,
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Both before and after the change, developers can populate an optional
&gt;&gt; `locale` data field with their preferred languages. Before this change, the
&gt;&gt; UA could use this language information however it wanted. This resulted in
&gt;&gt; UAs generally ignoring this field because SPC is a browser feature and to
&gt;&gt; align with other related browser features (e.g., WebAuthn), it would use
&gt;&gt; the browser language. After this change, if the field is set, the UA will
&gt;&gt; try to match the browser language with the developer provided list of
&gt;&gt; languages. If there's a match, there is no change; however, if there is no
&gt;&gt; match, the UA will return a locale mismatch error to the developer. The
&gt;&gt; intent behind this change is that the developer supplies strings for the
&gt;&gt; SPC dialog, and the language of those strings might not match the rest of
&gt;&gt; the dialog. This allows the developer to guarantee that the language of the
&gt;&gt; strings they provide matches the dialog's language.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Addison Phillip's concerns were not fully addressed but we have developer
&gt;&gt; support
&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/issues/343#issuecomment-5415886806"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/issues/343#issuecomment-5415886806&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; for this change. In addition, we opened an issue
&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/i18n-request/issues/324"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/i18n-request/issues/324&lt;/a&gt;&gt; with the i18n
&gt;&gt; community, and they told us they would review our PR for the spec change by
&gt;&gt; the end of September
&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/i18n-request/issues/324#issuecomment-5526812106"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/i18n-request/issues/324#issuecomment-5526812106&lt;/a&gt;&gt;.
&gt;&gt; It never ended up getting reviewed and after numerous attempts to ask for a
&gt;&gt; review (as well as inviting them to join our WPWG meeting on Oct 8th) we
&gt;&gt; received no response, so we decided to go ahead with the spec change so the
&gt;&gt; developer can begin testing the changes.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; On Mon, Oct 19, 2026 at 7:36 PM Alex Russell &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="285b44414f405c4451060606684b405a4745415d4506475a4f"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; The &quot;Explainer&quot; here is pretty thin, and I'm not sure I understand the
&gt;&gt;&gt; before/after code developers would generally write. Also, it wasn't clear
&gt;&gt;&gt; to me if Addison Phillip's comments were fully addressed; can you perhaps
&gt;&gt;&gt; comment on those aspects?
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/issues/343#issuecomment-5457268443"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/issues/343#issuecomment-5457268443&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Best,
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Alex
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; On Thursday, October 15, 2026 at 7:08:36 AM UTC-7 Chromestatus wrote:
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Contact emails*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="27434655504e495e09090967444f55484a4e524a09485540"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Explainer*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/issues/343"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/issues/343&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Specification*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://w3c.github.io/secure-payment-confirmation/#dom-securepaymentconfirmationrequest-locale"&gt;https://w3c.github.io/secure-payment-confirmation/#dom-securepaymentconfirmationrequest-locale&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Design docs*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/issues/343"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/issues/343&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/i18n-request/issues/324"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/i18n-request/issues/324&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/pull/345"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/pull/345&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Summary*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Updates Secure Payment Confirmation's `locale` data field to return a
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Not Supported DOMException if none of the language tags provided in the
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; field match the language used by the Secure Payment Confirmation's dialog.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; If the field is not set or empty, this validation is skipped. This helps
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; web developers with matching the language of the data that they are
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; supplying to Secure Payment Confirmation with the dialog.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Blink component*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Blink&gt;Payments
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EPayments%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EPayments%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Web Feature ID*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; secure-payment-confirmation
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://webstatus.dev/features/secure-payment-confirmation"&gt;https://webstatus.dev/features/secure-payment-confirmation&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Motivation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; This feature amends Secure Payment Confirmation so that web developers
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; can align the language of data elements that they supply to Secure Payment
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Confirmation with the language used by the Secure Payment Confirmation
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; dialog. Currently web developers can provide a list of language tags for
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Secure Payment Confirmation to use in their dialog. But Secure Payment
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Confirmation does not use this list because it is not feasible for the
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; browser to support all languages and the Secure Payment Confirmation is a
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; browser feature so it should use the browser language to be consistent with
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; other browser features. By returning an error when none of the language
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; tags provided match Secure Payment Confirmation's language, web developers
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; are able to retry with different language tags (while updating the language
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; of their supplied data elements) until they get a match.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Initial public proposal*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/issues/343"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/issues/343&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Search tags*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; spc &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="http:///features#tags:spc"&gt;http:///features#tags:spc&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *TAG review*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *TAG review status*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Not applicable
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Goals for experimentation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; None
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Risks*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Interoperability and Compatibility*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; This feature updates the behaviour of an existing field. If the
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; previous behaviour was implemented by other browser but this new behaviour
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; is not, then there is an interoperability risk of the browsers behaving
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; differently with the same request.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Gecko*: N/A (&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/570"&gt;https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/570&lt;/a&gt;) 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Firefox
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; haven't implemented SPC yet so the update to the locale field is not
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; relevant.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *WebKit*: N/A (&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/30"&gt;https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/30&lt;/a&gt;) 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Safari
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; haven't implemented SPC yet so the update to the locale field is not
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; relevant.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Web developers*: Positive (
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/issues/343#issuecomment-5415886806"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/issues/343#issuecomment-5415886806&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; ) &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://www.w3.org/2026/08/13-wpwg-minutes.html"&gt;https://www.w3.org/2026/08/13-wpwg-minutes.html&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://www.w3.org/2026/09/10-wpwg-minutes.html"&gt;https://www.w3.org/2026/09/10-wpwg-minutes.html&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://www.w3.org/2026/10/08-wpwg-minutes.html"&gt;https://www.w3.org/2026/10/08-wpwg-minutes.html&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Other signals*:
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *WebView application risks*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Does this intent deprecate or change behavior of existing APIs, such
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; that it has potentially high risk for Android WebView-based applications?
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Debuggability*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Web developers should be able to create Secure Payment Confirmation
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; requests with or without matching locales, thus no changes are needed in
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; devtools.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Will this feature be supported on all six Blink platforms (Windows,
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Mac, Linux, ChromeOS, Android, and Android WebView)?*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; No
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; The locale validation will only be added to platforms that support
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Secure Payment Confirmation which are currently only Android, macOS, and
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Windows.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Is this feature fully tested by web-platform-tests
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md"&gt;https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md&lt;/a&gt;&gt;?*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; No
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Web platform tests are in development. They are delayed due to the lack
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; of support to change the browser locale language which is needed for this
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; feature.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Flag name on about://flags*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; enable-spc-locale-validation
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Finch feature name*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; SecurePaymentConfirmationLocaleValidation
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Rollout plan*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Will ship enabled for all users
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Requires code in //chrome?*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; False
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Tracking bug*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://crbug.com/535278878"&gt;https://crbug.com/535278878&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Launch bug*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://launch.corp.google.com/launch/4489220"&gt;https://launch.corp.google.com/launch/4489220&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Measurement*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; A new SecurePaymentConfirmation.LocaleOutcome will be created and used
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; to track the usage and outcomes (match vs no-match) of the field.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Availability expectation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; The locale validation for Secure Payment Confirmation will only be
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; available in Chromium browsers for the foreseeable future.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Estimated milestones*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Shipping on desktop 154
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Shipping on Android 154
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Anticipated spec changes*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Open questions about a feature may be a source of future web compat or
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; interop issues. Please list open issues (e.g. links to known github issues
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; in the project for the feature specification) whose resolution may
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; introduce web compat/interop risk (e.g., changing to naming or structure of
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; the API in a non-backward-compatible way).
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/i18n-request/issues/324"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/i18n-request/issues/324&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/issues/343"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/issues/343&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/pull/345"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/secure-payment-confirmation/pull/345&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Link to entry on the Chrome Platform Status*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5126146013396992?gate=4803300429004800"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5126146013396992?gate=4803300429004800&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Links to previous Intent discussions*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Intent to Prototype:
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/6a7ccbd5.dc132f77.2e13a8.0cd1.GAE%40google.com"&gt;https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/6a7ccbd5.dc132f77.2e13a8.0cd1.GAE%40google.com&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; This intent message was generated by Chrome Platform Status
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com"&gt;https://chromestatus.com&lt;/a&gt;&gt;.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;

-- 
