&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-align"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-align&lt;/a&gt; is a larger test suite, are all of
&gt;&gt;&gt; the relevant tests already passing? (I tried to dig in but
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt.fyi/issues/5203"&gt;https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt.fyi/issues/5203&lt;/a&gt; got in the
&gt;&gt;&gt; way of filtering.)
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; And thanks for filing
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/4282"&gt;https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/4282&lt;/a&gt;!
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; On Wed, Oct 14, 2026 at 8:04 PM 'Celeste Pan' via blink-dev &lt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="30525c595e1e1e1e705358425f5d59455d1e5f4257"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Contact emails
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="2142444d44520f0f0f614c4842534e524e47550f424e4c"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="c4a5a8a9eaeaea84a9ada7b6abb7aba2b0eaa7aba9"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="85fce4ebe9ecabababc5e8ece6f7eaf6eae3f1abe6eae8"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;,
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="076a6f68292929476a6e647568746861732964686a"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Explainer
&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Specification
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/pull/14539"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/pull/14539&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Summary
&gt;&gt;&gt; It was resolved in the CSSWG that we should introduce the flow-start/end
&gt;&gt;&gt; keywords as value aliases for the existing flex-start/end keywords. These
&gt;&gt;&gt; are needed for alignment in the case of placement reversals.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; flow-start in CSS Grid-Lanes would indicate the starting edge of the
&gt;&gt;&gt; container at which placement begins, which is useful in the case where
&gt;&gt;&gt; placement is reversed (`fill-reverse`, `track-reverse`, discussed in this
&gt;&gt;&gt; CSSWG issue: [css-grid-3][masonry] item-flow row vs. column in masonry
&gt;&gt;&gt; layouts · Issue #12803 · w3c/csswg-drafts). Because these are acting as
&gt;&gt;&gt; value aliases, we expect flex-start/end to follow the logical directions in
&gt;&gt;&gt; Grid Lanes, as well, which will expand the definition of these keywords
&gt;&gt;&gt; from only applying special behavior in flexbox to applying to any layout
&gt;&gt;&gt; mode whose logical start/end is different from its physical start/end.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; For serialization, if either flex-start/end or flow-start/end is used,
&gt;&gt;&gt; the returned serialized value should be flow-start/end.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Blink component
&gt;&gt;&gt; Blink&gt;CSS
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ECSS%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ECSS%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Web Feature ID
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/4282"&gt;https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/4282&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://webstatus.dev/features/https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/4282"&gt;https://webstatus.dev/features/https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/4282&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Motivation
&gt;&gt;&gt; In grid-lanes, there is currently no alignment keyword to allow us to
&gt;&gt;&gt; align based on the start of content placement when reversal is present;
&gt;&gt;&gt; instead, we can only currently use the logical container start/end.  We
&gt;&gt;&gt; wanted a keyword that behaves the way flex-start/end does in flexbox
&gt;&gt;&gt; containers.  Introducing flow-start/end allows us to align based on content
&gt;&gt;&gt; placement start/end, and aliasing it to flex-start/end means that we can
&gt;&gt;&gt; have the same keyword used across flexbox, grid, and grid-lanes layout with
&gt;&gt;&gt; the same expected behavior.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Initial public proposal
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12803"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12803&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; TAG review
&gt;&gt;&gt; N/A - the feature is an alias to an existing API and documentation of
&gt;&gt;&gt; its resolution can be found in this CSSWG issue:
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12803"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12803&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12803"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12803&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; TAG review status
&gt;&gt;&gt; N/A
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Goals for experimentation
&gt;&gt;&gt; None
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Risks
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;    - Interoperability and Compatibility
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; For serialization, if either flex-start/end  or flow-start/end  is used,
&gt;&gt;&gt; the returned serialized value should be flow-start/end.  This could
&gt;&gt;&gt; introduce compatibility concerns for sites that rely on the existing
&gt;&gt;&gt; serialization of flex-start/end.  Because of this, we plan to use a second
&gt;&gt;&gt; flag to introduce a separate gate for the new serialization behavior of
&gt;&gt;&gt; flex-start/end so that if we receive reports of site breakages as a result,
&gt;&gt;&gt; we can disable the serialization behavior separately from the new keywords.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Gecko*: Positive (
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1455#issuecomment-5839398061"&gt;https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1455#issuecomment-5839398061&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; )
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *WebKit*: No Signal (
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/723"&gt;https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/723&lt;/a&gt;)
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Web developers*: No Signal (While we don't have direct signals from
&gt;&gt;&gt; developers on flow-start/end, flex-start/end are used by a number of sites
&gt;&gt;&gt; to achieve alignment based on placement direction, thus, because grid lanes
&gt;&gt;&gt; also supports reversals, a more generic keyword allows us to extend the
&gt;&gt;&gt; behavior to other layout modes to achieve the same use cases that
&gt;&gt;&gt; developers are able to achieve in flexbox today)
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Other signals*:
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;    - WebView application risks: N/A
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Debuggability
&gt;&gt;&gt; They will have same debugging capabilities as flex-start/end.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Will this feature be supported on all six Blink platforms (Windows, Mac,
&gt;&gt;&gt; Linux, ChromeOS, Android, and Android WebView)?
&gt;&gt;&gt; Yes
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Is this feature fully tested by
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md"&gt;https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; web-platform-tests
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md"&gt;https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; ?
&gt;&gt;&gt; Yes
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-align?label=master&amp;label=experimental&amp;aligned&amp;q=css-align"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-align?label=master&amp;label=experimental&amp;aligned&amp;q=css-align&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Flag name on about://flags
&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Finch feature name
&gt;&gt;&gt; CSSFlowStartAndEnd,CSSFlowStartAndEndSerialization
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Rollout plan
&gt;&gt;&gt; Will ship enabled for all users
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Requires code in //chrome?
&gt;&gt;&gt; False
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Tracking bug
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/555299635"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues/555299635&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Estimated milestones
&gt;&gt;&gt;    Dev Trial                                     157
&gt;&gt;&gt;    Shipping                                     158
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Anticipated spec changes
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Open questions about a feature may be a source of future web compat or
&gt;&gt;&gt; interop issues. Please list open issues (e.g. links to known github issues
&gt;&gt;&gt; in the project for the feature specification) whose resolution may
&gt;&gt;&gt; introduce web compat/interop risk (e.g., changing to naming or structure of
&gt;&gt;&gt; the API in a non-backward-compatible way).*
&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
