&lt;pre&gt;FYI I had LGTM3'd on Oct 7 but apparently dropped blink-dev from the
thread. Sorry!&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;


On Thu, Oct 1, 2026 at 5:02 AM Philip Jägenstedt &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="492f2626676767092a213b2624203c2467263b2e"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
wrote:

&gt; LGTM2
&gt;
&gt; I see that &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/whatwg/bluetooth/pull/672"&gt;https://github.com/whatwg/bluetooth/pull/672&lt;/a&gt; is approved, can
&gt; it be merged now?
&gt;
&gt; On Wed, Sep 30, 2026 at 5:24 PM Chris Harrelson &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="abc8c3d9c2d8858585ebc8c3d9c4c6c2dec685c4d9cc"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt; wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; LGTM1
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; On Tue, Sep 29, 2026 at 10:20 AM Helmut Januschka &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="325a58535c4741511c1c1c72555f535b5e1c515d5f"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Contact emails*
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="81e9ebe0eff4f2e2afafafc1e6ece0e8edafe2eeec"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Explainer*
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebBluetoothCG/web-bluetooth/pull/672"&gt;https://github.com/WebBluetoothCG/web-bluetooth/pull/672&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Specification*
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://pr-preview.s3.amazonaws.com/hjanuschka/web-bluetooth/pull/672.html#bluetoothremotegattserver"&gt;https://pr-preview.s3.amazonaws.com/hjanuschka/web-bluetooth/pull/672.html#bluetoothremotegattserver&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Summary*
&gt;&gt;&gt; BluetoothRemoteGATTServer inherits from EventTarget, exposing the
&gt;&gt;&gt; standard addEventListener(), removeEventListener(), and dispatchEvent()
&gt;&gt;&gt; methods. This enables connection-level events to be dispatched directly on
&gt;&gt;&gt; the GATT server.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Blink component*
&gt;&gt;&gt; Blink&gt;Bluetooth
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EBluetooth%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EBluetooth%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Web Feature ID*
&gt;&gt;&gt; web-bluetooth &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://webstatus.dev/features/web-bluetooth"&gt;https://webstatus.dev/features/web-bluetooth&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Motivation*
&gt;&gt;&gt; BluetoothRemoteGATTServer represents an active GATT connection and needs
&gt;&gt;&gt; to host connection-level events. Making it an EventTarget gives web
&gt;&gt;&gt; applications the standard event-listener API needed by events such as the
&gt;&gt;&gt; separately proposed maxwritewithoutresponsesizechanged event.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Initial public proposal*
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebBluetoothCG/web-bluetooth/pull/672"&gt;https://github.com/WebBluetoothCG/web-bluetooth/pull/672&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Search tags*
&gt;&gt;&gt; web-bluetooth &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/features#tags:web-bluetooth"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/features#tags:web-bluetooth&lt;/a&gt;&gt;,
&gt;&gt;&gt; bluetooth &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/features#tags:bluetooth"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/features#tags:bluetooth&lt;/a&gt;&gt;,
&gt;&gt;&gt; eventtarget &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/features#tags:eventtarget"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/features#tags:eventtarget&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *TAG review*
&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *TAG review status*
&gt;&gt;&gt; Issues addressed
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Goals for experimentation*
&gt;&gt;&gt; None
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Risks*
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Interoperability and Compatibility*
&gt;&gt;&gt; This is a small but observable change to an existing interface. Existing
&gt;&gt;&gt; content could be affected if it relies on BluetoothRemoteGATTServer not
&gt;&gt;&gt; having addEventListener(), relies on an instance not being an instanceof
&gt;&gt;&gt; EventTarget, or enumerates inherited properties and does not expect
&gt;&gt;&gt; EventTarget members. The affected surface is limited to sites using Web
&gt;&gt;&gt; Bluetooth. Firefox and Safari do not currently implement Web Bluetooth.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Gecko*: Negative (
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/95"&gt;https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/95&lt;/a&gt;) Firefox does
&gt;&gt;&gt; not implement Web Bluetooth. The citation is Mozilla's position on the
&gt;&gt;&gt; overall Web Bluetooth API, not a separate position on this inheritance
&gt;&gt;&gt; change.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *WebKit*: Oppose (
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/570"&gt;https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/570&lt;/a&gt;) Safari does
&gt;&gt;&gt; not implement Web Bluetooth. The citation is WebKit's position on the
&gt;&gt;&gt; overall Web Bluetooth API, not a separate position on this inheritance
&gt;&gt;&gt; change.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Web developers*: Positive this is a small preparation feature for the
&gt;&gt;&gt; larger demanded: &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40265040"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40265040&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Other signals*: The WebBluetoothCG specification change is approved in
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebBluetoothCG/web-bluetooth/pull/672"&gt;https://github.com/WebBluetoothCG/web-bluetooth/pull/672&lt;/a&gt; but has not
&gt;&gt;&gt; yet merged.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Ergonomics*
&gt;&gt;&gt; Low. EventTarget is the standard event-listener pattern used throughout
&gt;&gt;&gt; the web platform. The change does not add synchronous work, thread
&gt;&gt;&gt; constraints, or performance-sensitive behavior. It prepares
&gt;&gt;&gt; BluetoothRemoteGATTServer to expose connection-level events alongside the
&gt;&gt;&gt; existing Web Bluetooth APIs.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Activation*
&gt;&gt;&gt; Low. Developers use the standard addEventListener() API and need no
&gt;&gt;&gt; polyfill or library. This inheritance change alone does not require
&gt;&gt;&gt; application changes; developers use it when connection-level events are
&gt;&gt;&gt; exposed.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Security*
&gt;&gt;&gt; This exposes only the standard EventTarget methods on an existing Web
&gt;&gt;&gt; Bluetooth object. It does not grant access to additional devices, services,
&gt;&gt;&gt; characteristics, data, or operations. Existing Web Bluetooth permission,
&gt;&gt;&gt; secure-context, service allowlist, blocklist, and Permissions Policy
&gt;&gt;&gt; protections remain unchanged.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *WebView application risks*
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Does this intent deprecate or change behavior of existing APIs, such
&gt;&gt;&gt; that it has potentially high risk for Android WebView-based applications?
&gt;&gt;&gt; None. Android WebView does not expose Web Bluetooth, so
&gt;&gt;&gt; BluetoothRemoteGATTServer is not available there.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Debuggability*
&gt;&gt;&gt; The inherited EventTarget methods and registered listeners are
&gt;&gt;&gt; inspectable using the existing DevTools Console and event-listener tools.
&gt;&gt;&gt; No dedicated DevTools panel or protocol support is required.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Will this feature be supported on all six Blink platforms (Windows,
&gt;&gt;&gt; Mac, Linux, ChromeOS, Android, and Android WebView)?*
&gt;&gt;&gt; No
&gt;&gt;&gt; Supported on Windows, macOS, Linux, ChromeOS, and Android wherever Web
&gt;&gt;&gt; Bluetooth is available. Chrome on iOS and Android WebView do not expose Web
&gt;&gt;&gt; Bluetooth.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Is this feature fully tested by web-platform-tests
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md"&gt;https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md&lt;/a&gt;&gt;?*
&gt;&gt;&gt; No
&gt;&gt;&gt; Chromium's global interface listing tests verify that
&gt;&gt;&gt; BluetoothRemoteGATTServer inherits from EventTarget:
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/web_tests/webexposed/global-interface-listing.html"&gt;https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/web_tests/webexposed/global-interface-listing.html&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; The Web Bluetooth WPT IDL harness will cover the same inheritance after
&gt;&gt;&gt; specification PR 672 merges and the generated Web Bluetooth IDL snapshot is
&gt;&gt;&gt; updated:
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/bluetooth/bidi/idl/idlharness.tentative.https.window.js"&gt;https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/bluetooth/bidi/idl/idlharness.tentative.https.window.js&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebBluetoothCG/web-bluetooth/pull/672"&gt;https://github.com/WebBluetoothCG/web-bluetooth/pull/672&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Flag name on about://flags*
&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Finch feature name*
&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Non-finch justification*
&gt;&gt;&gt; Blink cannot conditionally enable Web IDL inheritance. The inheritance
&gt;&gt;&gt; change has therefore been isolated into a standalone implementation CL and
&gt;&gt;&gt; shipping intent.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Rollout plan*
&gt;&gt;&gt; Will ship enabled for all users
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Requires code in //chrome?*
&gt;&gt;&gt; False
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Tracking bug*
&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40265040"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40265040&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Measurement*
&gt;&gt;&gt; No dedicated UseCounter is added for the inheritance change. Exposure
&gt;&gt;&gt; and use remain associated with the existing web-bluetooth Web Feature ID.
&gt;&gt;&gt; The change is also covered by Chromium's global interface listing tests.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Estimated milestones*
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Shipping on desktop
&gt;&gt;&gt; 157
&gt;&gt;&gt; Shipping on Android
&gt;&gt;&gt; 157
&gt;&gt;&gt; Shipping on WebView
&gt;&gt;&gt; 157
&gt;&gt;&gt; Shipping on iOS
&gt;&gt;&gt; 157
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Anticipated spec changes*
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Open questions about a feature may be a source of future web compat or
&gt;&gt;&gt; interop issues. Please list open issues (e.g. links to known github issues
&gt;&gt;&gt; in the project for the feature specification) whose resolution may
&gt;&gt;&gt; introduce web compat/interop risk (e.g., changing to naming or structure of
&gt;&gt;&gt; the API in a non-backward-compatible way).
&gt;&gt;&gt; The inheritance change is included in WebBluetoothCG PR 672. The PR is
&gt;&gt;&gt; approved and no further substantive changes to this inheritance are
&gt;&gt;&gt; anticipated, but it must merge before shipping.
