&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22Re%5C%3A+%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Intent+to+Ship%5C%3A+SVG+Path+Data+API%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Ship: SVG Path Data API&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Stephen+Chenney%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Stephen Chenney&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20261026" rel="nofollow"&gt;Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:54:48 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;On Wed, Oct 21, 2026 at 12:43 PM Chromestatus &lt;
&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="ff9e9bd1d1d1bf9c8dd28c8b9e8b8a8cd19e8f8f8c8f908b929e9693d19c9092"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

&gt; *Contact emails*
&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="afd9c6ddcec3c6dfdadd818181efc2c6ccddc0dcc0c9db81ccc0c2"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="86f5f2e3f0a8a8a8c6ebefe5f4e9f5e9e0f2a8e5e9eb"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Explainer*
&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/MicrosoftEdge/MSEdgeExplainers/blob/main/SVG/SVGPathDataAPI/explainer.md"&gt;https://github.com/MicrosoftEdge/MSEdgeExplainers/blob/main/SVG/SVGPathDataAPI/explainer.md&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Specification*
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://w3c.github.io/svgwg/specs/paths/#InterfaceSVGPathData"&gt;https://w3c.github.io/svgwg/specs/paths/#InterfaceSVGPathData&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Design docs*
&gt;
&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uCVUqYGKgsCCu7LEtEdO3Yuea-MT-I2XsU6Eoe3mlQI/edit?usp=sharing"&gt;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uCVUqYGKgsCCu7LEtEdO3Yuea-MT-I2XsU6Eoe3mlQI/edit?usp=sharing&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Summary*
&gt; Adds structured JavaScript access to SVG path data through three methods
&gt; on SVGPathElement: getPathData() reads the path as an array of {type,
&gt; values} objects containing each segment's command and numeric parameters.
&gt; setPathData() updates the path from such an array, getPathSegmentAtLength()
&gt; returns the segment at a specified distance along the path. These methods
&gt; let developers inspect, edit, and construct paths without manually parsing
&gt; or serializing the d attribute. The optional getPathData({normalize: true})
&gt; setting simplifies path data to absolute move, line, cubic Bézier, and
&gt; close commands (M, L, C, and Z). All three APIs operate on the base value
&gt; of the d attribute, not CSS-computed or animated values.


Out of curiosity, how are the ellptical arc path commands converted to M,
L, C and Z? The spec doesn't say anything about the necessary approximation.


&gt; *Blink component*
&gt; Blink&gt;SVG
&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ESVG%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ESVG%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Web Feature ID*
&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;
&gt; *Motivation*
&gt; In Chromium, inspecting or modifying individual SVG path segments requires
&gt; parsing and serializing the d attribute string, often using third-party
&gt; libraries. This makes tasks such as path animation, hit-testing, and
&gt; programmatic path construction unnecessarily complex and error-prone. The
&gt; previous SVGPathSegList API was removed in Chromium 48 because of its
&gt; complex live mutation model, numerous factory methods, and underspecified
&gt; edge cases. Developers have since relied on polyfills to restore structured
&gt; access. Implementing the SVG Working Group’s replacement API provides a
&gt; simpler, standardized way to read and modify path segments without custom
&gt; string parsing or polyfills.
&gt;
&gt; *Initial public proposal*
&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;
&gt; *TAG review*
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1292"&gt;https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1292&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *TAG review status*
&gt; Pending
&gt;
&gt; *Goals for experimentation*
&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Risks*
&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Interoperability and Compatibility*
&gt; Low risk. The feature adds new methods to SVGPathElement that developers
&gt; can feature-detect before use. Representatives from Chromium, Firefox,
&gt; WebKit, and the web developer community contributed to the API design
&gt; through the SVG Working Group.
&gt;
&gt; *Gecko*: Shipped/Shipping (
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1934525"&gt;https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1934525&lt;/a&gt;) Firefox 137 shipped
&gt; the feature in April 2025.
&gt;
&gt; *WebKit*: No signal (
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/731"&gt;https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/731&lt;/a&gt;)
&gt;
&gt; *Web developers*: Positive (&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40441025"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40441025&lt;/a&gt;) 45
&gt; users upvoted this Chromium issue. A widely used polyfill exists:
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/jarek-foksa/path-data-polyfill"&gt;https://github.com/jarek-foksa/path-data-polyfill&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Other signals*:
&gt;
&gt; *WebView application risks*
&gt;
&gt; Does this intent deprecate or change behavior of existing APIs, such that
&gt; it has potentially high risk for Android WebView-based applications?
&gt; None. The feature adds new methods to SVGPathElement that developers can
&gt; feature-detect before use.
&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Debuggability*
&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;
&gt; *Will this feature be supported on all six Blink platforms (Windows, Mac,
&gt; Linux, ChromeOS, Android, and Android WebView)?*
&gt; Yes
&gt;
&gt; *Is this feature fully tested by web-platform-tests
&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md"&gt;https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md&lt;/a&gt;&gt;?*
&gt; Yes
&gt;
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/svg/path/interfaces?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/svg/path/interfaces?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Flag name on about://flags*
&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;
&gt; *Finch feature name*
&gt; SVGPathDataAPI
&gt;
&gt; *Rollout plan*
&gt; Will ship enabled for all users
&gt;
&gt; *Requires code in //chrome?*
&gt; False
&gt;
&gt; *Tracking bug*
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40441025"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40441025&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Measurement*
&gt; Use counters include: - SVGPathElementGetPathData -
&gt; SVGPathElementSetPathData -SVGPathElementGetPathSegmentAtLength
&gt;
&gt; *Availability expectation*
&gt; The feature is available in Chromium and Firefox for the foreseeable
&gt; future. Microsoft proposed this feature as a focus area for Interop 2027:
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/web-platform-tests/interop/issues/1469"&gt;https://github.com/web-platform-tests/interop/issues/1469&lt;/a&gt;, which if
&gt; accepted, could help extend support to additional browsers.
&gt;
&gt; *Adoption expectation*
&gt; The feature replaces a popular polyfill that developers use today with
&gt; thousands of downloads per week. The Chromium issue has 45 votes.
&gt; Developers have made inquiries, asking when it will become available.
&gt;
&gt; *Adoption plan*
&gt; MDN already documents this feature. Given the existing developer interest,
&gt; the feature's adoption should grow organically.
&gt;
&gt; *Non-OSS dependencies*
&gt;
&gt; Does the feature depend on any code or APIs outside the Chromium open
&gt; source repository and its open-source dependencies to function?
&gt; None.
&gt;
&gt; *Estimated milestones*
&gt; Shipping on desktop 159
&gt; Shipping on Android 159
&gt; Shipping on WebView 159
&gt;
&gt; *Anticipated spec changes*
&gt;
&gt; Open questions about a feature may be a source of future web compat or
&gt; interop issues. Please list open issues (e.g. links to known github issues
&gt; in the project for the feature specification) whose resolution may
&gt; introduce web compat/interop risk (e.g., changing to naming or structure of
&gt; the API in a non-backward-compatible way).
&gt; None. Representatives from Chromium, Firefox, WebKit, and the web
&gt; developer community contributed to the API design through the W3C SVG WG.
&gt;
&gt; *Link to entry on the Chrome Platform Status*
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/4787972240179200?gate=4660848254648320"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/4787972240179200?gate=4660848254648320&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Links to previous Intent discussions*
&gt; Intent to Prototype:
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/KUXP153MB161031AEB43220B1ADB9B41AC1112%40KUXP153MB1610.APCP153.PROD.OUTLOOK.COM"&gt;https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/KUXP153MB161031AEB43220B1ADB9B41AC1112%40KUXP153MB1610.APCP153.PROD.OUTLOOK.COM&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt;
&gt; This intent message was generated by Chrome Platform Status
&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com"&gt;https://chromestatus.com&lt;/a&gt;&gt;.
&gt;
&gt; --
