&gt;&gt; *Availability expectation*
&gt;&gt; Feature is available on Web Platform Baseline within 12 months of launch
&gt;&gt; in Chrome. Safari is mid-implementation and Mozilla has shown positive
&gt;&gt; signals towards implementation.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Adoption expectation*
&gt;&gt; Feature is considered best practice for providing `accent-color` styling
&gt;&gt; as a value keyword within 12 months of reaching Web Platform baseline.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Adoption plan*
&gt;&gt; We will drive availability through the existing CSSWG standardization and
&gt;&gt; coordination with other browser vendors. For adoption, we will update MDN
&gt;&gt; and Chrome developer documentation to recommend AccentColor and
&gt;&gt; AccentColorText as the preferred way to reuse the effective accent-color
&gt;&gt; value in authored CSS.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Non-OSS dependencies*
&gt;&gt; *Does the feature depend on any code or APIs outside the Chromium open
&gt;&gt; source repository and its open-source dependencies to function?*
&gt;&gt; No.
