&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22Re%5C%3A+%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Re%5C%3A+Intent+to+Ship%5C%3A+Background+layer+count+independence%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Re: [blink-dev] Re: Intent to Ship: Background layer count independence&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Chris+Harrelson%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Chris Harrelson&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20261027" rel="nofollow"&gt;Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:23:44 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;LGTM2

On Tue, Oct 27, 2026 at 7:08 PM Alex Russell &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="f487989d939c80988ddadadab4979c869b999d8199da9b8693"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
wrote:&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

&gt; LGTM1; thanks for the note about interop risk, makes this easier to
&gt; approve.
&gt;
&gt; On Monday, October 26, 2026 at 2:56:32 PM UTC-7 Chromestatus wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Contact emails*
&gt;&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="553f3330273b343b7b7b7b153c3234393c347b363a38"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Specification*
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/#linked-properties"&gt;https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/#linked-properties&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Summary*
&gt;&gt; Makes the computed value of the background-* longhands keep the number of
&gt;&gt; comma-separated values the author specified, instead of repeating or
&gt;&gt; truncating it to the background-image layer count. Repeating and truncating
&gt;&gt; are used-value behavior: &quot;The computed values of the coordinating list
&gt;&gt; properties are not affected by such truncation or repetition.&quot; This feature
&gt;&gt; would implement the behavior defined in the
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/"&gt;https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/&lt;/a&gt; Appendix A.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Blink component*
&gt;&gt; Blink&gt;CSS
&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ECSS%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ECSS%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Web Feature ID*
&gt;&gt; background &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://webstatus.dev/features/background"&gt;https://webstatus.dev/features/background&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Motivation*
&gt;&gt; The behavior defined in the &quot;Appendix A: Coordinating List-Valued
&gt;&gt; Properties&quot; of the CSS Values And Units L4 specification has been discussed
&gt;&gt; recently and agreed that it should stand. This makes Chrome the only
&gt;&gt; browser diverging in the specified behavior.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Initial public proposal*
&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *TAG review*
&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *TAG review status*
&gt;&gt; Not applicable
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Goals for experimentation*
&gt;&gt; None
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Risks*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Interoperability and Compatibility*
&gt;&gt; The new behavior this feature provides is implemented already by Firefox
&gt;&gt; and Safari, so it's Chrome catching up in this case; hence, the interop
&gt;&gt; risk is zero. Regarding compatibility, making the background-* properties
&gt;&gt; align &quot;coordinated list group&quot; is what matches the current specified
&gt;&gt; behavior, which the CSSWG agreed on keep. Some engines implemented weird
&gt;&gt; truncation rules, that's why there were some WPT not following the spec.
&gt;&gt; The resolution [1] was to update the tests and observe whether any compat
&gt;&gt; issue appears in the next months. [1]
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12791#issuecomment-4040285092"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12791#issuecomment-4040285092&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Gecko*: Shipped/Shipping Firefox was the only one implementing the
&gt;&gt; behavior defined in the spec.
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12791#issuecomment-4040285092"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12791#issuecomment-4040285092&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *WebKit*: Shipped/Shipping (
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/safari-technology-preview-release-notes/stp-release-246"&gt;https://developer.apple.com/documentation/safari-technology-preview-release-notes/stp-release-246&lt;/a&gt;)
&gt;&gt;  See
&gt;&gt; the bug &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=315771"&gt;https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=315771&lt;/a&gt; for details
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Web developers*: No signals
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Other signals*:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *WebView application risks*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Does this intent deprecate or change behavior of existing APIs, such that
&gt;&gt; it has potentially high risk for Android WebView-based applications?
&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Debuggability*
&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Will this feature be supported on all six Blink platforms (Windows, Mac,
&gt;&gt; Linux, ChromeOS, Android, and Android WebView)?*
&gt;&gt; Yes
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Is this feature fully tested by web-platform-tests
&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md"&gt;https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md&lt;/a&gt;&gt;?*
&gt;&gt; Yes
&gt;&gt; *
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-backgrounds/parsing?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-backgrounds/parsing?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt; *
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-backgrounds/animations/background-position-interpolation.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-backgrounds/animations/background-position-interpolation.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt; *
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-backgrounds/animations/background-size-interpolation.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-backgrounds/animations/background-size-interpolation.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt; *
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-masking/parsing?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-masking/parsing?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Flag name on about://flags*
&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Finch feature name*
&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Non-finch justification*
&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Rollout plan*
&gt;&gt; Will ship enabled for all users
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Requires code in //chrome?*
&gt;&gt; False
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Tracking bug*
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40855581"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40855581&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Estimated milestones*
&gt;&gt; Shipping on desktop 159
&gt;&gt; Shipping on Android 159
&gt;&gt; Shipping on WebView 159
&gt;&gt; Shipping on iOS 159
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Anticipated spec changes*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Open questions about a feature may be a source of future web compat or
&gt;&gt; interop issues. Please list open issues (e.g. links to known github issues
&gt;&gt; in the project for the feature specification) whose resolution may
&gt;&gt; introduce web compat/interop risk (e.g., changing to naming or structure of
&gt;&gt; the API in a non-backward-compatible way).
&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Link to entry on the Chrome Platform Status*
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5144333908049920?gate=6114123363516416"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5144333908049920?gate=6114123363516416&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Links to previous Intent discussions*
&gt;&gt; Intent to Prototype:
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/eny3Exk0b8w/m/HiXscXadAgAJ"&gt;https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/eny3Exk0b8w/m/HiXscXadAgAJ&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; This intent message was generated by Chrome Platform Status
&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com"&gt;https://chromestatus.com&lt;/a&gt;&gt;.
&gt;&gt;
&gt; --
&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups
&gt; &quot;blink-dev&quot; group.
&gt; To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an
&gt; email to &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="f0929c999e9bdd949586db859e838592839382dededeb09398829f9d99859dde9f8297"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;.
&gt; To view this discussion visit
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/1a9a7278-d5a2-42a7-8556-2086d23e5fa9n%40chromium.org"&gt;https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/1a9a7278-d5a2-42a7-8556-2086d23e5fa9n%40chromium.org&lt;/a&gt;
&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/1a9a7278-d5a2-42a7-8556-2086d23e5fa9n%40chromium.org?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer"&gt;https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/1a9a7278-d5a2-42a7-8556-2086d23e5fa9n%40chromium.org?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt; .
&gt;

