&lt;pre style="margin: 0em;"&gt; LGTM3
On 10/28/26 5:22 a.m., Chris Harrelson wrote: &lt;/pre&gt;&lt;blockquote style="border-left: #5555EE solid 0.2em; margin: 0em; padding-left: 0.85em"&gt;&lt;pre style="margin: 0em;"&gt; LGTM2&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;tt&gt;On Tue, Oct 27, 2026 at 7:07 PM Alex Russell &lt;/tt&gt;&lt;tt&gt;&lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="0e7d626769667a62772020204e6d667c6163677b6320617c69"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote: &lt;/tt&gt;&lt;pre style="margin: 0em;"&gt;
LGTM1; thanks for bringing us into conformance with the spec in a way that solves a real problem for devleopers.
On Friday, October 23, 2026 at 10:23:52 AM UTC-7 &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="086963716d7a2626264865616b7a677b676e7c266b6765"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt; wrote:
*Contact emails* &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="f6979d8f93849394d8d8d8b69b9f95849985999082d895999b"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
*Specification* &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-4/#css-system-colors"&gt;https://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-4/#css-system-colors&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://nam06.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2FTR%2Fcss-color-4%2F%23css-system-colors&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cakyereboah%40microsoft.com%7C4e8179bfc54e4c5f71ce08df29770355%7C72f988bf86f141af91ab2d7cd011db47%7C1%7C0%7C639275263355947969%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=bn%2BZS%2FTPPurMIPKv%2FVMTsLP2bdHKrG9T6%2BcY5ReRXpY%3D&amp;reserved=0"&gt;https://nam06.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2FTR%2Fcss-color-4%2F%23css-system-colors&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cakyereboah%40microsoft.com%7C4e8179bfc54e4c5f71ce08df29770355%7C72f988bf86f141af91ab2d7cd011db47%7C1%7C0%7C639275263355947969%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=bn%2BZS%2FTPPurMIPKv%2FVMTsLP2bdHKrG9T6%2BcY5ReRXpY%3D&amp;reserved=0&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
*Summary* `AccentColor` and `AccentColorText` reflect the element's effective `accent-color` value instead of only platform-provided system accent colors. This allows CSS to reference the same colors used by `accent-color` styling, making it easier to keep custom styling consistent with form controls and other accented UI. It aligns Chromium's behavior with the CSS Color Module Level 4 specification.
*Blink component* Blink&gt;CSS
&lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://nam06.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fissues.chromium.org%2Fissues%3Fq%3Dcustomfield1222907%3A%2522Blink%253ECSS%2522&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cakyereboah%40microsoft.com%7C4e8179bfc54e4c5f71ce08df29770355%7C72f988bf86f141af91ab2d7cd011db47%7C1%7C0%7C639275263355961615%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=%2FrOBhNA%2FtkSP%2F4hyYzb8PGvHOogw2%2B8dPMdUb8ZjmPM%3D&amp;reserved=0"&gt;https://nam06.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fissues.chromium.org%2Fissues%3Fq%3Dcustomfield1222907%3A%2522Blink%253ECSS%2522&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cakyereboah%40microsoft.com%7C4e8179bfc54e4c5f71ce08df29770355%7C72f988bf86f141af91ab2d7cd011db47%7C1%7C0%7C639275263355961615%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=%2FrOBhNA%2FtkSP%2F4hyYzb8PGvHOogw2%2B8dPMdUb8ZjmPM%3D&amp;reserved=0&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
*Web Feature ID* accentcolor
&lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://nam06.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwebstatus.dev%2Ffeatures%2Faccentcolor&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cakyereboah%40microsoft.com%7C4e8179bfc54e4c5f71ce08df29770355%7C72f988bf86f141af91ab2d7cd011db47%7C1%7C0%7C639275263355977495%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=p%2FkBdXHRL5kxO89K2nARX2JxANP06XnWkaZWeJ56tjQ%3D&amp;reserved=0"&gt;https://nam06.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwebstatus.dev%2Ffeatures%2Faccentcolor&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cakyereboah%40microsoft.com%7C4e8179bfc54e4c5f71ce08df29770355%7C72f988bf86f141af91ab2d7cd011db47%7C1%7C0%7C639275263355977495%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=p%2FkBdXHRL5kxO89K2nARX2JxANP06XnWkaZWeJ56tjQ%3D&amp;reserved=0&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
*Motivation* Currently, `AccentColor` and `AccentColorText` keywords have been implemented in a limited capacity for Chromium. They reflect the OS' chosen system accent color when `accent-color` is set to `auto` in an installed web app, and return a default value otherwise. The CSSWG resolved that the keywords should reflect the value of `accent-color`, allowing developers to use the keywords for intuitive styling of elements. Without this change, the keywords provide no additional value unless being used specifically for a system accent color.
*Initial public proposal* [css-color-4] [css-ui-4] `color: AccentColor; accent-color: currentColor` cycle · Issue #14192 · w3c/csswg-drafts
&lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://nam06.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fw3c%2Fcsswg-drafts%2Fissues%2F14192%23issuecomment-5202877510&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cakyereboah%40microsoft.com%7C4e8179bfc54e4c5f71ce08df29770355%7C72f988bf86f141af91ab2d7cd011db47%7C1%7C0%7C639275263355994546%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=tIgdVWj6wmIADgr1%2BOW0VrMmLjlBNAV8MU4cdc8ZYMo%3D&amp;reserved=0"&gt;https://nam06.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fw3c%2Fcsswg-drafts%2Fissues%2F14192%23issuecomment-5202877510&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cakyereboah%40microsoft.com%7C4e8179bfc54e4c5f71ce08df29770355%7C72f988bf86f141af91ab2d7cd011db47%7C1%7C0%7C639275263355994546%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=tIgdVWj6wmIADgr1%2BOW0VrMmLjlBNAV8MU4cdc8ZYMo%3D&amp;reserved=0&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
*TAG review* This resolution is a minor update to an existing API, it is a final published standard and is actively being worked on by another browser.
*TAG review status* Not applicable
*Risks* *Interoperability and Compatibility* Low risk. This change aligns Chromium with the CSS Color Module Level 4 specification for `AccentColor` and `AccentColorText`. Sites using these keywords may observe different color values when `accent-color` is specified, but the new behavior matches the standardized definition of the keywords and improves interoperability.
