&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Re%5C%3A+Intent+to+Ship%5C%3A+WebTransport+Datagram+readable+stream+type%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;[blink-dev] Re: Intent to Ship: WebTransport Datagram readable stream type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22%27Monica+Chintala%27+via+blink%5C-dev%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;'Monica Chintala' via blink-dev&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20261028" rel="nofollow"&gt;Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:20:14 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;Thanks, Alex. We cannot measure the exact intersection, but existing 
UseCounters provide an upper bound. Access to  WebTransport.datagrams  
peaked at 0.0126% of page loads over the last 30 days. For the common 
 getReader({mode: &quot;byob&quot;}) pattern, the upper bound is 0.00232%, fewer than 
1 in 43,000 page loads.&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

The actual intersection may be lower because the BYOB counter covers all 
APIs. Affected applications can preserve the current behavior with 
 datagramsReadableType: &quot;bytes&quot;, and the change remains Finch-controlled 
for rollback.

On Wednesday, October 28, 2026 at 8:32:01 AM UTC-7 Alex Russell wrote:

&gt; Is there an upper bound for potential breakage? Do we have metrics for 
&gt; total use of datagram readable streams w/ BYOB behaviours?
&gt;
&gt; On Wednesday, October 28, 2026 at 7:35:15 AM UTC-7 Monica Chintala wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; We don’t have a metric for this exact usage pattern. The affected case is 
&gt;&gt; limited to applications requesting a BYOB reader without opting into 
&gt;&gt;  &quot;bytes&quot;.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Default readers continue to work unchanged. Applications using BYOB can 
&gt;&gt; preserve the existing Chromium behavior by adding: {datagramsReadableType: 
&gt;&gt; &quot;bytes&quot;}
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; This option can be added before rollout and works with both the old and 
&gt;&gt; new behavior. Firefox and Safari stable already use the new default. The 
&gt;&gt; rollout is Finch-controlled, so we can restore the previous default without 
&gt;&gt; a new release if compatibility problems are reported.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; On Tuesday, October 27, 2026 at 12:02:26 PM UTC-7 Alex Russell wrote:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; What's the potential for breakage, given that we're changing default 
&gt;&gt;&gt; behavior? Do our histograms tell us the fraction of pageloads that would be 
&gt;&gt;&gt; affected?
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Best,
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Alex
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; On Wednesday, October 21, 2026 at 1:52:53 PM UTC-7 Chromestatus wrote:
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Contact emails*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="ed9f84c3c3c3ad8e859f8280849880c3829f8a"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="412c2e2f286f6f6f012c2822332e322e27356f222e2c"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Explainer*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/webtransport/blob/main/explainer.md"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/webtransport/blob/main/explainer.md&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Specification*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://www.w3.org/TR/webtransport/#dom-webtransportoptions-datagramsreadabletype"&gt;https://www.w3.org/TR/webtransport/#dom-webtransportoptions-datagramsreadabletype&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;  
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Summary*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Adds the  WebTransportOptions.datagramsReadableType  constructor 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; option. By default, incoming WebTransport Datagrams are exposed through a 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; default  ReadableStream . Applications that require BYOB reading can 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; request a readable byte stream by setting  datagramsReadableType: &quot;bytes&quot; 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; . 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Blink component*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Blink&gt;Network&gt;WebTransport 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ENetwork%3EWebTransport%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ENetwork%3EWebTransport%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Web Feature ID*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; webtransport &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://webstatus.dev/features/webtransport"&gt;https://webstatus.dev/features/webtransport&lt;/a&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Motivation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; WebTransport Datagrams are discrete messages rather than an 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; undifferentiated byte sequence. A readable byte stream can lose empty 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Datagrams and can lose message boundaries when BYOB reads use a minimum 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; byte count spanning multiple Datagrams. Making a default  ReadableStream  
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; the default preserves Datagram boundaries and empty Datagrams. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Applications 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; that benefit from BYOB allocation control can explicitly opt into the 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; byte-stream behavior. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Initial public proposal*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *TAG review*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Not applicable — this is a small incremental addition within the 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; existing WebTransport specification. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *TAG review status*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Not applicable
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Goals for experimentation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; None 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Risks*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Interoperability and Compatibility*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Interoperability risk is low to medium. The API and default-stream 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; behavior are defined in the WebTransport specification and covered by WPT. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Firefox already uses a default non-byte stream when the option is omitted, 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; but does not yet support the explicit  &quot;bytes&quot;  mode in current public 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; test 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; runs. Compatibility risk is mitigated by runtime gating. Chromium 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; historically exposed the Datagram readable as a byte stream, so enabling 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; the feature changes the default behavior: existing applications using a 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; BYOB reader without specifying  datagramsReadableType: &quot;bytes&quot; would fail. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Applications using ordinary readers continue to receive  Uint8Array  
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; chunks 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Gecko*: Positive (&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2007755"&gt;https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2007755&lt;/a&gt;) 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Firefox 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; is implementing datagramsReadableType: &quot;bytes&quot; and BYOB Datagram reads
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *WebKit*: In development (
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319830"&gt;https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319830&lt;/a&gt;) WebKit main implements 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; the standardized datagramsReadableType option
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Web developers*: Positive (
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/web-platform-tests/interop/issues/1121"&gt;https://github.com/web-platform-tests/interop/issues/1121&lt;/a&gt;) The Interop 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; 2026 WebTransport proposal received 28 👍 reactions. Developers also 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; reported active WebTransport use and significant cross-engine differences.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Other signals*:
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Ergonomics*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Low. The default stream better matches Datagram message semantics. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Applications needing BYOB allocation control must explicitly opt into 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;  &quot;bytes&quot; , making the semantic tradeoff visible in application code.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Activation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; The main activation risk is existing Chromium-specific code assuming 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; that  transport.datagrams.readable  always supports BYOB readers. Such 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; applications must explicitly request  datagramsReadableType: &quot;bytes&quot; . The 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; feature remains experimentally gated while compatibility and 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; interoperability are evaluated.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Security*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Low. The option changes only the JavaScript stream adapter used to 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; expose already-received Datagrams. It does not provide additional network 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; access, expose new information, or alter WebTransport’s secure-context and 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; connection security requirements.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *WebView application risks*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Does this intent deprecate or change behavior of existing APIs, such 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; that it has potentially high risk for Android WebView-based applications? 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Low. The implementation is cross-platform Blink code and requires no 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; WebView-specific integration. The primary compatibility consideration is 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; the same as Chrome: applications using a BYOB reader must explicitly 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; request  datagramsReadableType: &quot;bytes&quot; . 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Debuggability*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; No feature-specific DevTools UI is required. Applications can inspect 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; whether  datagrams.readable  supports BYOB by attempting to acquire a BYOB 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; reader. Existing WebTransport logging, NetLog, and DevTools network 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; diagnostics remain available for connection and Datagram issues. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Will this feature be supported on all six Blink platforms (Windows, 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Mac, Linux, ChromeOS, Android, and Android WebView)?*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Yes 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Yes. Implemented in cross-platform Blink code without platform-specific 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; dependencies. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Is this feature fully tested by web-platform-tests 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md"&gt;https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md&lt;/a&gt;&gt;?*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Yes 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/webtransport/datagrams.https.any.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/webtransport/datagrams.https.any.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Flag name on about://flags*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; chrome://flags/#enable-experimental-web-platform-features 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Finch feature name*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; WebTransportDatagramsReadableType 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Rollout plan*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Will ship enabled for all users
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Requires code in //chrome?*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; False
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Tracking bug*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/547572475"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues/547572475&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Availability expectation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; WebKit has implemented the option and corresponding default-stream 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; behavior in its main branch. Firefox implements the default non-byte 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; stream 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; behavior, although explicit  &quot;bytes&quot; /BYOB mode does not yet pass current 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; public WPT runs. Broad availability is expected as implementations 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; converge 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; on the WebTransport specification.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Adoption expectation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Adoption is expected mainly among WebTransport applications that use 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; BYOB readers or need reliable preservation of Datagram message boundaries. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Most applications using ordinary readers require no code changes. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Adoption plan*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Adoption is expected through WebTransport documentation and Interop 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; 2026 visibility. Existing Chromium applications using BYOB readers will 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; need to explicitly set  datagramsReadableType: &quot;bytes&quot;  when the feature 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; is 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; enabled.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Estimated milestones*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Shipping on desktop 159 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; DevTrial on desktop 155 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Shipping on Android 159 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; DevTrial on Android 155 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Shipping on WebView 159 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Anticipated spec changes*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Open questions about a feature may be a source of future web compat or 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; interop issues. Please list open issues (e.g. links to known github issues 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; in the project for the feature specification) whose resolution may 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; introduce web compat/interop risk (e.g., changing to naming or structure 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; of 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; the API in a non-backward-compatible way). 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; None currently anticipated. The option and default-stream behavior are 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; already defined in the WebTransport specification.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Link to entry on the Chrome Platform Status*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5148774971342848?gate=5517621058469888"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5148774971342848?gate=5517621058469888&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Links to previous Intent discussions*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Intent to Prototype: 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/6aa86417.edf999b6.71d4e.0a07.GAE%40google.com"&gt;https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msgid/blink-dev/6aa86417.edf999b6.71d4e.0a07.GAE%40google.com&lt;/a&gt;
