&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;*Contact emails* &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="790a0d1c10575757391a110b1614100c1457160b1e"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
*Explainer* &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/mediasession/pull/312"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/mediasession/pull/312&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;
*Specification* &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://w3c.github.io/mediasession/#dom-mediasession-setmicrophoneactive"&gt;https://w3c.github.io/mediasession/#dom-mediasession-setmicrophoneactive&lt;/a&gt;
*Summary* Updates navigator.mediaSession.setMicrophoneActive() and navigator.mediaSession.setCameraActive() to return a Promise&lt;undefined&gt; instead of undefined, matching the W3C Media Session specification. In a fully active document, the returned promise resolves with undefined; if the associated document is not fully active, it returns a promise rejected with an InvalidStateError DOMException.
*Blink component* Blink&gt;Media&gt;Session &lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EMedia%3ESession%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EMedia%3ESession%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
*Web Feature ID* media-session &lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://webstatus.dev/features/media-session"&gt;https://webstatus.dev/features/media-session&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
*Motivation* When MediaSession.setMicrophoneActive() and MediaSession.setCameraActive() were originally specified and shipped in Chrome 93, their WebIDL return type was void (undefined). The W3C Media Session specification was subsequently updated (&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/mediasession/pull/312"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/mediasession/pull/312&lt;/a&gt;) so that both methods return Promise&lt;undefined&gt; to support user agents that apply a capture pause policy or prompt the user asynchronously. Updating Chromium's implementation to return Promise&lt;undefined&gt; aligns Chrome with the W3C Media Session specification and fixes 4 failing subtests in WPT's mediasession/idlharness.window.html.
*Initial public proposal* *No information provided*
*TAG review* N/A — This is a minor spec-compliance update to the return type (undefined -&gt; Promise&lt;undefined&gt;) of two already-shipped MediaSession methods, already specified in the W3C Media Session Working Draft ( &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/mediasession/pull/312"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/mediasession/pull/312&lt;/a&gt;) and shipped in Safari.
*TAG review status* Not applicable
*Goals for experimentation* None
*Risks*
*Interoperability and Compatibility* Compatibility risk is very low. Existing callers that ignore the return value of setMicrophoneActive() and setCameraActive() are unaffected because the returned promise always resolves with undefined in an active document (so fire-and-forget callers will not encounter unhandled promise rejections). The promise only rejects with InvalidStateError when called on a MediaSession whose associated Document is no longer fully active (such as a detached iframe), or with TypeError when called with too few arguments or an invalid receiver per WebIDL rules for promise-returning operations. Interoperability is improved, as Safari already ships Promise&lt;undefined&gt; for both methods and Firefox is implementing the same WebIDL signature.
*Gecko*: Positive (&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/504"&gt;https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/504&lt;/a&gt; )
*WebKit*: Shipped/Shipping (&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=277421"&gt;https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=277421&lt;/a&gt;) Shipped in Safari 18.4
*Web developers*: No signals N/A — Minor spec-compliance fix to return Promise&lt;undefined&gt; instead of undefined.
*Other signals*:
*WebView application risks*
Does this intent deprecate or change behavior of existing APIs, such that it has potentially high risk for Android WebView-based applications? *No information provided*
*Debuggability* *No information provided*
*Will this feature be supported on all six Blink platforms (Windows, Mac, Linux, ChromeOS, Android, and Android WebView)?* Yes
*Is this feature fully tested by web-platform-tests &lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md"&gt;https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md&lt;/a&gt;&gt;?* Yes &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/mediasession/idlharness.window.html"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/mediasession/idlharness.window.html&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/mediasession/setmicrophoneactive.html"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/mediasession/setmicrophoneactive.html&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/mediasession/setcameraactive.html"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/mediasession/setcameraactive.html&lt;/a&gt;
*Flag name on about://flags* *No information provided*
*Finch feature name* *No information provided*
*Non-finch justification* Changing a WebIDL method's return type from void to Promise&lt;undefined&gt; cannot be guarded behind a runtime feature flag in Blink's generated bindings without changing the IDL return type to 'any' and losing WebIDL's automatic promise-rejection wrapping for invalid arguments/receivers. Compatibility risk is negligible because the returned promise always resolves in an active document.
*Rollout plan* Will ship enabled for all users
*Requires code in //chrome?* False
*Tracking bug* &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://crbug.com/576328036"&gt;https://crbug.com/576328036&lt;/a&gt;
*Estimated milestones* Shipping on desktop 159 Shipping on Android 159
*Anticipated spec changes*
Open questions about a feature may be a source of future web compat or interop issues. Please list open issues (e.g. links to known github issues in the project for the feature specification) whose resolution may introduce web compat/interop risk (e.g., changing to naming or structure of the API in a non-backward-compatible way). *No information provided*
*Link to entry on the Chrome Platform Status* &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5188639100370944?gate=5532358353747968"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5188639100370944?gate=5532358353747968&lt;/a&gt;
