&gt;&gt;&gt; On Monday, October 19, 2026 at 4:19:14 PM UTC-7 &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="87f3efe8eae6f4e4ebeea9a9a9c7e0eae6eeeba9e4e8ea"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt; 
&gt;&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; not clear how this interfaces with w3c, but here are a few threats I 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; found partly from AI.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    - *Keystroke Redirection &amp; Phishing (Focus Theft):* Embedded 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    third-party content can silently pull focus away from the main page 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; input 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    fields. If a user is typing sensitive information (e.g., 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    credentials, credit card numbers, or search queries), their keystrokes 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; can 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    be redirected into an embedded iframe or form without visual or 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; immediate 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    notice. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    1 &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5179186249465856"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5179186249465856&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    2 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#all/%23thread-f:1879048351712254581%7Cmsg-f:1879503045256153924"&gt;https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#all/%23thread-f:1879048351712254581%7Cmsg-f:1879503045256153924&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    - *Accessibility Disruption for Assistive Technologies:* Screen 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    readers and keyboard-only navigation depend heavily on stable focus. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    Unprompted focus changes forcibly relocate the reading or keyboard 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    focus, confusing visually or mobility-impaired users and preventing 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; them 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    from navigating predictably. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    3 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://www.webaccessibility.com/resource-library/best-practice/?bestPractice=801"&gt;https://www.webaccessibility.com/resource-library/best-practice/?bestPractice=801&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    - *Keyboard Navigation Hijacking:* Users attempting to navigate 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    forms or pages via keyboard shortcuts or Tab keys can be trapped or 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    thrown off course if a script continually pulls focus back to a 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; specific 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    element. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    3 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://www.webaccessibility.com/resource-library/best-practice/?bestPractice=801"&gt;https://www.webaccessibility.com/resource-library/best-practice/?bestPractice=801&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    - *UI Flickering &amp; Performance Degradation:* When multiple scripts 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    or embedded frames aggressively run scripts (e.g., using 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    element.focus(), window.focus(), or blur event polling) to reclaim 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    or maintain focus, it results in visible screen flickering and erratic 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; user 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    interface behavior. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    1 &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5179186249465856"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5179186249465856&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    2 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#all/%23thread-f:1879048351712254581%7Cmsg-f:1879503045256153924"&gt;https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#all/%23thread-f:1879048351712254581%7Cmsg-f:1879503045256153924&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    - *Unwanted Modals &amp; Dialog Interruptions:* Scripts can force focus 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    into programmatic popups or dialogs (dialog.showModal(), popover 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    focusing, or autofocus), disrupting the workflow without any 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    preceding user action or gesture. 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    1 &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5179186249465856"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5179186249465856&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;    
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Also note that focus may become another threat with folding screens 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; which now have an open possible with focus that could be major confusion.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Peace ..tom jones
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
