&gt;
&gt; *Motivation*
&gt; Currently there is no web standard way to control whether text decorations 
&gt; (underlines, overlines, line-throughs) appear over whitespace characters. 
&gt; Authors commonly want to suppress the underline under leading/trailing 
&gt; spaces in inline elements, but CSS provides no mechanism for this. The 
&gt; `text-decoration-skip-spaces` property fills this gap, allowing precise 
&gt; control over decoration rendering around whitespace. This is useful for 
&gt; navigation menus, links, and any text where the decoration should visually 
&gt; attach only to non-space characters. 
