&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;LGTM2, +1 this is exciting, thanks for making it happen!

On Mon, Sep 14, 2026 at 5:13 PM Alex Russell &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="e3908f8a848b978f9acdcdcda3808b918c8e8a968ecd8c9184"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
wrote:&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

&gt; LGTM1; exciting feature, happy to see it come to the web. Thanks for
&gt; making it happen, Adam.
&gt;
&gt; On Thursday, September 10, 2026 at 12:34:58 PM UTC-7 Daniel Bratell wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; Good point about not spamming them. The features that are being
&gt;&gt; implemented now, would they have been in the 2024 spec? If so, then that
&gt;&gt; link is just what we needed to see. If not, maybe a blanket &quot;All the new
&gt;&gt; Interop 2026 WebTransport features&quot; question?
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; /Daniel
&gt;&gt; On 2026-09-10 10:21, Adam Rice wrote:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Request: Please file a Mozilla positions issue.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; There's an existing issue for WebTransport as a whole here:
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/167"&gt;https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/167&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Because it is part of interop 2026
&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://web.dev/blog/interop-2026#the_webtransport_api"&gt;https://web.dev/blog/interop-2026#the_webtransport_api&lt;/a&gt;&gt;, we are going
&gt;&gt; to shipping a lot of WebTransport features
&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/platform/runtime_enabled_features.json5?q=file:third_party%2Fblink%2Frenderer%2Fplatform%2Fruntime_enabled_features.json5%20WebTransport%20"&gt;https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/platform/runtime_enabled_features.json5?q=file:third_party%2Fblink%2Frenderer%2Fplatform%2Fruntime_enabled_features.json5%20WebTransport%20&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; that are already standardised in the next few months. If we file a Mozilla
&gt;&gt; position issue for all of them it may strike them as a DoS attack.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Will this feature be supported on all six Blink platforms (Windows,
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Mac, Linux, ChromeOS, Android, and Android WebView)? *No
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; All Blink platforms supported. Implemented in cross-platform code.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Do you mean &quot;yes&quot; for this question then?
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Sorry, yes. I've fixed it on chromestatus.com now.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; On Thu, 3 Sept 2026 at 00:19, Chris Harrelson &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="096a617b607a272727496a617b6664607c6427667b6e"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; One request and one question:
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Request: Please file a Mozilla positions issue.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Question below:
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; *Will this feature be supported on all six Blink platforms (Windows,
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Mac, Linux, ChromeOS, Android, and Android WebView)?*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; No
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; All Blink platforms supported. Implemented in cross-platform code.
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; Do you mean &quot;yes&quot; for this question then?
&gt;&gt;&gt;
