&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22Re%5C%3A+%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Intent+to+Prototype%5C%3A+Permissions+Policy+for+dedicated+and+shared+workers%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Prototype: Permissions Policy for dedicated and shared workers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Reilly+Grant%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Reilly Grant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20260917" rel="nofollow"&gt;Thu, 17 Sep 2026 10:01:01 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;I'm very excited to see this work progressing because developers could fix
a whole category of problems by adopting Shared Workers, but they are
currently blocked because the necessary APIs aren't available there.
Reilly Grant | Software Engineer | &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="314354585d1f1f1f715259435e5c58445c1f5e4356"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt; | Google Chrome
&lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://www.google.com/chrome"&gt;https://www.google.com/chrome&lt;/a&gt;&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;


On Thu, Sep 17, 2026 at 6:25 AM Chromestatus &lt;
&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="cfaeabe1e1e18facbde2bcbbaebbbabce1aebfbfbcbfa0bba2aea6a3e1aca0a2"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:

&gt; *Contact emails*
&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="a2c3ccd6cdcccbcdd1c3d0d68c8c8ce2c1cad0cdcfcbd7cf8ccdd0c5"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Explainer*
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/workers-permissions-policy"&gt;https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/workers-permissions-policy&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Specification*
&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;
&gt; *Summary*
&gt; Extend the Permissions Policy infrastructure to dedicated and shared
&gt; workers. Web developers will be able to delegate policy-controlled features
&gt; to dedicated and shared workers via Permissions Policy. This will enable
&gt; browsers to expose features gated behind Permissions Policy to workers.
&gt;
&gt; *Blink component*
&gt; Blink
&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Web Feature ID*
&gt; permissions-policy &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://webstatus.dev/features/permissions-policy"&gt;https://webstatus.dev/features/permissions-policy&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Motivation*
&gt; The goal of this proposal is to extend Permissions Policy to workers, in
&gt; order to enable shipping Permissions Policy gated capabilities to those
&gt; contexts. Note there are a number of proposals and use cases for extending
&gt; Web APIs that are currently gated behind Permissions Policy to workers (see
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/workers-permissions-policy#example-use-cases"&gt;https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/workers-permissions-policy#example-use-cases&lt;/a&gt;)
&gt; which have been blocked until because Permissions Policy does not yet work
&gt; in workers. This proposal aims at unblocking those.
&gt;
&gt; *Initial public proposal*
&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;
&gt; *Goals for experimentation*
&gt; None
&gt;
&gt; *Requires code in //chrome?*
&gt; False
&gt;
&gt; *Tracking bug*
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/u/1/issues/562705553"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/u/1/issues/562705553&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Estimated milestones*
&gt;
&gt; No milestones specified
&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Link to entry on the Chrome Platform Status*
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5073502741856256?gate=5148864016416768"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5073502741856256?gate=5148864016416768&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; This intent message was generated by Chrome Platform Status
&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com"&gt;https://chromestatus.com&lt;/a&gt;&gt;.
&gt;
