Explainer &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/scroll-snap-type-pair"&gt;https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/scroll-snap-type-pair&lt;/a&gt;
Specification &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scroll-snap-1"&gt;https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scroll-snap-1&lt;/a&gt;
Summary &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/9519"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/9519&lt;/a&gt; Add a &quot;pair&quot; keyword to scroll-snap-type. If used, when the container scroll snaps to an element on one axis, it should snap to the same element on the other axis. In the existing spec, the &quot;both&quot; keyword allows the scroll container to select snap targets in X and Y axes independently and snap to different targets.
Blink component Blink&gt;Scroll
Web Feature ID scroll-snap
Motivation See explainer
Initial public proposal &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/9519"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/9519&lt;/a&gt;
TAG review &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1271"&gt;https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/1271&lt;/a&gt;
