*Explainer* &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/issues/5071"&gt;https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/issues/5071&lt;/a&gt; &lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/issues/5071"&gt;https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/issues/5071&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
*Specification* &lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://www.w3.org/TR/webgpu/#dom-gpufeaturename-atomic-vec2u-min-max"&gt;https://www.w3.org/TR/webgpu/#dom-gpufeaturename-atomic-vec2u-min-max&lt;/a&gt; &lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://www.w3.org/TR/webgpu/#dom-gpufeaturename-atomic-vec2u-min-max"&gt;https://www.w3.org/TR/webgpu/#dom-gpufeaturename-atomic-vec2u-min-max&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
*Summary* Allows the use of 64-bit atomic minimum and maximum operations on `atomic&lt;vec2u&gt;` in WGSL. This provides WebGPU shader authors with a way to implement certain algorithms that use 64-bit atomics without requiring full support for 64-bit integers.
*Blink component* Blink&gt;WebGPU
&lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EWebGPU%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EWebGPU%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
*Web Feature ID* webgpu &lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://webstatus.dev/features/webgpu"&gt;https://webstatus.dev/features/webgpu&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
*Motivation* This provides WebGPU shader authors with a way to implement certain algorithms that use 64-bit atomics without requiring full support for 64-bit integers. Not every device that supports 64-bit atomics can support every atomic operation on these types, so this feature is scoped to the min and max operations to deliver broadest reach.
*Initial public proposal*
&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/blob/main/proposals/atomic-64-min-max.md"&gt;https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/blob/main/proposals/atomic-64-min-max.md&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/blob/main/proposals/atomic-64-min-max.md"&gt;https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/blob/main/proposals/atomic-64-min-max.md&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
*TAG review* /No information provided/
*TAG review status* Not applicable
*Goals for experimentation* None
*Risks*
*Interoperability and Compatibility* This feature has been approved in W3C GPU for the Web WG meetings including participants from Safari and Firefox.
&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/wiki/GPU-Web-2026%E2%80%9009%E2%80%9015-WGSL#add-limited-support-for-64-bit-atomics-5071"&gt;https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/wiki/GPU-Web-2026%E2%80%9009%E2%80%9015-WGSL#add-limited-support-for-64-bit-atomics-5071&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;&lt;a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/wiki/GPU-Web-2026%E2%80%9009%E2%80%9015-WGSL#add-limited-support-for-64-bit-atomics-5071"&gt;https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/wiki/GPU-Web-2026%E2%80%9009%E2%80%9015-WGSL#add-limited-support-for-64-bit-atomics-5071&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
