&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22%27Dan+Clark%27+via+blink%5C-dev%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;'Dan Clark' via blink-dev&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20260928" rel="nofollow"&gt;Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:02:03 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;Will both the embedding page and the page embedded in the &lt;iframe&gt; need to 
opt in to the trial for this to work? What happens if one opts-in but not 
the other?
I'm wondering if partners might have trouble working with the trial if they 
don't control both sides. Or is expected that devs opting into this 
experiment will control both the embedder and embedee pages and can opt in 
both?&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

-- Dan

