&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22Re%5C%3A+%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Intent+to+Extend+Experiment%5C%3A+Prefetch+activation+beacon%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Re: [blink-dev] Intent to Extend Experiment: Prefetch activation beacon&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Chris+Harrelson%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Chris Harrelson&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20261007" rel="nofollow"&gt;Wed, 07 Oct 2026 08:41:51 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;LGTM

On Tue, Oct 6, 2026 at 3:27 PM Chromestatus &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="c4a5a0eaeaea84a7b6e9b7b0a5b0b1b7eaa5b4b4b7b4abb0a9a5ada8eaa7aba9"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
wrote:&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

&gt; *Contact emails*
&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="9bfcb5b5b5dbfcf4f4fcf7feb5f8f4f6"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Explainer*
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/prefetch-activation-beacon"&gt;https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/prefetch-activation-beacon&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Specification*
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/prefetch-activation-beacon"&gt;https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/prefetch-activation-beacon&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Summary*
&gt; The on-prefetch-activation HTTP response header enables servers to specify
&gt; a telemetry endpoint that the browser notifies when a prefetched resource
&gt; is used for navigation. Developers gain a reliable signal to measure the
&gt; precision and performance impact of their prefetch strategies.
&gt;
&gt; *Blink component*
&gt; Blink&gt;Loader&gt;Preload
&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ELoader%3EPreload%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ELoader%3EPreload%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Web Feature ID*
&gt; Missing feature
&gt;
&gt; *TAG review*
&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;
&gt; *TAG review status*
&gt; Pending
&gt;
&gt; *Origin Trial Name*
&gt; PrefetchAndPrerenderActivationBeacon
&gt;
&gt; *Goals for experimentation*
&gt; We are going to start origin trial for the prefetch activation beacon to
&gt; evaluate whether it can reliably report all the user navigation when the
&gt; page is prefetched. We will compare the DAU and the query count with a
&gt; group not using the API and reports activation via javascript.
&gt;
&gt; *Chromium Trial Name*
&gt; PrefetchAndPrerenderActivationBeacon
&gt;
&gt; *Origin Trial documentation link*
&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/prefetch-activation-beacon"&gt;https://github.com/explainers-by-googlers/prefetch-activation-beacon&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *WebFeature UseCounter name*
&gt; kPrefetchAndPrerenderActivationBeacon
&gt;
&gt; *Risks*
&gt;
&gt;
&gt; *Interoperability and Compatibility*
&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;
&gt; *Gecko*: No signal
&gt;
&gt; *WebKit*: No signal
&gt;
