&gt;
&gt;&gt; LGTM1
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; On Wed, Sep 30, 2026 at 12:25 PM Hubert Chao &lt;&lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="a5cdc68b8b8be5c6cdd7cac8ccd0c88bcad7c2"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;&gt; wrote:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt; One thing that may not be clear: the plan here is to remove the header
&gt;&gt;&gt; directly without a deprecation trial.
&gt;&gt;&gt; On Wednesday, September 30, 2026 at 3:22:59 PM UTC-4 Chromestatus wrote:
&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Contact emails*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="f49c97dadadab4979c869b999d8199da9b8693"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Explainer*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Specification*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Summary*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; The Content Security Policy header treat-as-public-address was added as
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; part of Private Network Access to allow non-documents to declare themselves
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; as being in the public address space (
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wicg.github.io/private-network-access/#csp"&gt;https://wicg.github.io/private-network-access/#csp&lt;/a&gt;). It is primarily
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; useful for testing.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/WICG/private-network-access/issues/88"&gt;https://github.com/WICG/private-network-access/issues/88&lt;/a&gt; highlights
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; some issues with this header, and the decision was made to remove this
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; header instead of moving it somewhere else. For testing use cases, the
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; --ip-address-space-overrides command line flag can be used. This header was
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; only ever implemented in Chromium; Firefox has never implemented this
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; header and has no plans to. Safari has not implemented Private Network
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Access or Local Network Access and so does not have the header either.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Blink component*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Blink &gt; SecurityFeature &gt; LocalNetworkAccess
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%20%3E%20SecurityFeature%20%3E%20LocalNetworkAccess%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%20%3E%20SecurityFeature%20%3E%20LocalNetworkAccess%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Web Feature ID*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; local-network-access
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://webstatus.dev/features/local-network-access"&gt;https://webstatus.dev/features/local-network-access&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Motivation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Header does not fit well into Content Security Policy, and it was
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; deemed unnecessary given the alternative of using
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; `--ip-address-space-overrides` Metrics show this is barely used:
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/metrics/feature/timeline/popularity/5983"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/metrics/feature/timeline/popularity/5983&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Initial public proposal*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Goals for experimentation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; None
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Debuggability*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Requires code in //chrome?*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; False
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
