&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="2c4a4a450202026c41454f5e435f434a58024f4341"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="3b575e541515157b565258495448545d4f15585456"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Explainer*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/ffiori/webappsec-permissions-policy/blob/focus-without-user-activation-explainer/policies/focus-without-user-activation.md"&gt;https://github.com/ffiori/webappsec-permissions-policy/blob/focus-without-user-activation-explainer/policies/focus-without-user-activation.md&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Specification*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#focus-without-user-activation-feature"&gt;https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#focus-without-user-activation-feature&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Summary*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Gives embedders control over programmatic focus from embedded content 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; via the `focus-without-user-activation` permissions policy. When the 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; policy 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; is denied for the initiating frame, programmatic focus changes (from 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; `element.focus()`, `autofocus`, `window.focus()`, and the focusing steps 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; for dialogs and popovers) are blocked unless that frame has transient 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; user 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; activation or focus is already within its subtree. This does not prevent 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; dialogs or popovers from opening. User-initiated focus such as clicking 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; or 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; tabbing is never affected. The policy can be set via a 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; `Permissions-Policy` 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; HTTP response header or the iframe `allow` attribute. Focus delegation 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; is 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; supported: a parent frame that has focus can programmatically pass focus 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; to 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; a child iframe, even if the child has the policy denied, and once a 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; frame 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; has focus it can move focus within its own subtree.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Blink component*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Blink&gt;FeaturePolicy 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EFeaturePolicy%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3EFeaturePolicy%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Web Feature ID*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Missing feature
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Motivation*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Embedded third-party content such as ads, widgets, and iframes can 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; programmatically steal input focus from the top-level page without any 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; user 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; interaction, silently redirecting keystrokes and creating security and 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; accessibility problems. This was originally reported by engineers 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; working 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; on advertising security for large publishers. Today developers have no 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; reliable way to prevent it: the sandbox attribute disables JavaScript 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; entirely, breaking most embedded content, and JavaScript 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; focus-reclaiming 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; hacks using blur listeners or polling are unreliable, cause visible 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; focus 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; flickering, and do not scale across multiple iframes. This policy 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; provides 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; fine-grained, declarative control over programmatic focus from embedded 
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; content.
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; *Initial public proposal*
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-permissions-policy/issues/273"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-permissions-policy/issues/273&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;
