&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="msgHead"&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;
&lt;span class="subject"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=subject:%22Re%5C%3A+%5C%5Bblink%5C-dev%5C%5D+Re%5C%3A+Intent+to+Ship%5C%3A+WebTransport+anticipated+concurrent+incoming+streams%22&amp;o=newest" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Re: [blink-dev] Re: Intent to Ship: WebTransport anticipated concurrent incoming streams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="darkgray font13"&gt;
&lt;span class="sender pipe"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=from:%22Alex+Russell%22" rel="nofollow"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="author" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"&gt;&lt;span itemprop="name"&gt;Alex Russell&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="date"&gt;&lt;a href="/search?l=blink-dev@chromium.org&amp;q=date:20261021" rel="nofollow"&gt;Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:14:48 -0700&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div itemprop="articleBody" class="msgBody"&gt;

&lt;pre&gt;LGTM3

On Wednesday, October 21, 2026 at 8:49:10 AM UTC-7 Daniel Bratell wrote:&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;pre&gt;

&gt; LGTM2
&gt;
&gt; /Daniel
&gt; On 2026-10-21 17:31, Yoav Weiss (@Shopify) wrote:
&gt;
&gt; LGTM1
&gt;
&gt; On Tuesday, October 20, 2026 at 11:08:15 PM UTC+2 Chromestatus wrote:
&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Contact emails*
&gt;&gt; &lt;a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="f0869282899899dededeb09d9993829f839f9684de939f9d"&gt;[email&#160;protected]&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Explainer*
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/webtransport/issues/544"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/webtransport/issues/544&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/w3c/webtransport/pull/574"&gt;https://github.com/w3c/webtransport/pull/574&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Specification*
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://w3c.github.io/webtransport/#web-transport-configuration"&gt;https://w3c.github.io/webtransport/#web-transport-configuration&lt;/a&gt; 
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Summary*
&gt;&gt; Allows WebTransport applications to indicate how many incoming streams 
&gt;&gt; they expect to have open at once. Constructor hints configure the initial 
&gt;&gt; QUIC stream allowance, reducing the risk that a server that needs high 
&gt;&gt; stream concurrency is blocked by the initial stream limit. 
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Blink component*
&gt;&gt; Blink&gt;Network&gt;WebTransport 
&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ENetwork%3EWebTransport%22"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues?q=customfield1222907:%22Blink%3ENetwork%3EWebTransport%22&lt;/a&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Web Feature ID*
&gt;&gt; webtransport &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://webstatus.dev/features/webtransport"&gt;https://webstatus.dev/features/webtransport&lt;/a&gt;&gt; 
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Motivation*
&gt;&gt; Some WebTransport applications expect a server to open many streams at 
&gt;&gt; once. If the initial QUIC stream allowance is too low, the server must wait 
&gt;&gt; for more stream credit before opening additional streams, adding avoidable 
&gt;&gt; latency or limiting the number of open streams. Constructor hints let the 
&gt;&gt; application state its expected stream count when creating the connection, 
&gt;&gt; so the browser can advertise an appropriate initial allowance. Values above 
&gt;&gt; the required minimum are preserved; values below 100 do not reduce the 
&gt;&gt; effective allowance because the specification requires clients to initially 
&gt;&gt; permit at least 100 streams of each type. 
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Initial public proposal*
&gt;&gt; *No information provided*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *TAG review*
&gt;&gt; This is a small incremental addition to an existing feature which is 
&gt;&gt; already standardized. 
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *TAG review status*
&gt;&gt; Not applicable
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Goals for experimentation*
&gt;&gt; None 
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Risks*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Interoperability and Compatibility*
&gt;&gt; Compatibility risk is low because this is an additive API. Existing sites 
&gt;&gt; that do not use the new names are unaffected. Interoperability risk is low 
&gt;&gt; to moderate: WebKit implements these specific members, while Firefox 
&gt;&gt; supports WebTransport but does not currently expose them. 
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Gecko*: Positive (&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2007825"&gt;https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2007825&lt;/a&gt;) 
&gt;&gt; Firefox 
&gt;&gt; supports WebTransport, but not these two anticipated-incoming-stream 
&gt;&gt; members. Implementation work is in progress, no shipping milestone is 
&gt;&gt; announced.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *WebKit*: Shipped/Shipping (&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://commits.webkit.org/303419@main"&gt;https://commits.webkit.org/303419@main&lt;/a&gt;) 
&gt;&gt; Implemented 
&gt;&gt; in WebKit revision 303419@main and shipped in Safari 26.4, including Safari 
&gt;&gt; on iOS.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Web developers*: Positive (
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/web-platform-tests/interop/issues/1121"&gt;https://github.com/web-platform-tests/interop/issues/1121&lt;/a&gt;) The Interop 
&gt;&gt; 2026 WebTransport proposal received 28 positive reactions. Developers also 
&gt;&gt; reported active WebTransport use and significant cross-engine differences.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Other signals*:
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Ergonomics*
&gt;&gt; The constructor options are nullable unsigned-short hints and default to 
&gt;&gt; null. The corresponding attributes expose the currently stored values. 
&gt;&gt; [EnforceRange] rejects values outside the unsigned-short range. Values 
&gt;&gt; below 100 remain visible through the attributes but cannot reduce the 
&gt;&gt; effective initial stream allowance below the specification-required minimum.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Activation*
&gt;&gt; No permission or user activation is required beyond the existing 
&gt;&gt; WebTransport requirements. A site opts in by supplying either constructor 
&gt;&gt; option.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Security*
&gt;&gt; This does not grant a new capability or expose application data. It lets 
&gt;&gt; a site request a bounded initial stream allowance for its existing 
&gt;&gt; secure-context WebTransport connection. Stream credit does not eagerly 
&gt;&gt; allocate all streams.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *WebView application risks*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Does this intent deprecate or change behavior of existing APIs, such that 
&gt;&gt; it has potentially high risk for Android WebView-based applications? 
&gt;&gt; Low. The change is additive and does not modify behavior for applications 
&gt;&gt; that do not use the new options or attributes. The implementation uses the 
&gt;&gt; existing cross-platform WebTransport connection stack. 
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Debuggability*
&gt;&gt; The hints can be inspected through the JavaScript attributes. Existing 
&gt;&gt; DevTools and NetLog support for WebTransport and QUIC remains applicable. 
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Will this feature be supported on all six Blink platforms (Windows, Mac, 
&gt;&gt; Linux, ChromeOS, Android, and Android WebView)?*
&gt;&gt; Yes
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Is this feature fully tested by web-platform-tests 
&gt;&gt; &lt;&lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md"&gt;https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/testing/web_platform_tests.md&lt;/a&gt;&gt;?*
&gt;&gt; Yes 
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://wpt.fyi/results/webtransport/anticipated-concurrent-incoming-streams.https.any.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master"&gt;https://wpt.fyi/results/webtransport/anticipated-concurrent-incoming-streams.https.any.html?label=experimental&amp;label=master&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Flag name on about://flags*
&gt;&gt; enable-experimental-web-platform-features 
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Finch feature name*
&gt;&gt; WebTransportAnticipatedConcurrentIncomingStreams 
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Rollout plan*
&gt;&gt; Will ship enabled for all users
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Requires code in //chrome?*
&gt;&gt; False
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Tracking bug*
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/565837025"&gt;https://issues.chromium.org/issues/565837025&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Availability expectation*
&gt;&gt; The API is part of the W3C WebTransport specification and is implemented 
&gt;&gt; by WebKit/Safari. Firefox supports WebTransport but does not yet expose 
&gt;&gt; these specific members. Cross-browser availability is expected to improve 
&gt;&gt; as implementations converge on the current WebTransport specification.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Adoption expectation*
&gt;&gt; Adoption is expected among WebTransport applications whose servers need 
&gt;&gt; to create more than the minimum number of streams concurrently, including 
&gt;&gt; real-time communication, media, gaming, remote interaction, and multiplexed 
&gt;&gt; application protocols. Broader adoption will follow overall WebTransport 
&gt;&gt; usage.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Adoption plan*
&gt;&gt; No dedicated outreach campaign is planned. Adoption is expected through 
&gt;&gt; WebTransport documentation, examples, and client/server library support.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Non-OSS dependencies*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Does the feature depend on any code or APIs outside the Chromium open 
&gt;&gt; source repository and its open-source dependencies to function? 
&gt;&gt; No.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Estimated milestones*
&gt;&gt; Shipping on desktop 158 
&gt;&gt; DevTrial on desktop 151 
&gt;&gt; Shipping on Android 158 
&gt;&gt; DevTrial on Android 151 
&gt;&gt; Shipping on WebView 158 
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Anticipated spec changes*
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; Open questions about a feature may be a source of future web compat or 
&gt;&gt; interop issues. Please list open issues (e.g. links to known github issues 
&gt;&gt; in the project for the feature specification) whose resolution may 
&gt;&gt; introduce web compat/interop risk (e.g., changing to naming or structure of 
&gt;&gt; the API in a non-backward-compatible way). 
&gt;&gt; None known for these constructor options or attributes. The wider 
&gt;&gt; WebTransport specification continues to progress, but no known open issue 
&gt;&gt; requires a breaking change to these members before launch.
&gt;&gt;
&gt;&gt; *Link to entry on the Chrome Platform Status*
&gt;&gt; &lt;a  rel="nofollow" href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5089961022980096?gate=5533718100967424"&gt;https://chromestatus.com/feature/5089961022980096?gate=5533718100967424&lt;/a&gt;
&gt;&gt;
